Remove dead code found by the last sweeps (#158-#171)

Only unused imports, attributes, methods, arguments and commented-out
leftovers were deleted; no behaviour changed. Verified by rebuilding all
three shipped databases from the CanSNPer2-data source files: the sqlite
dumps and the tab exports are byte identical to the pre-change code, and
the Francisella end-to-end run (query Ames, five references,
progressiveMauve) gives the same SNP calls and the same not-called rows.

P4
- #158 SNPDatabase: the commented-out --add_node/--add_snp arguments were
  dropped; those flags were never implemented and --mod_file covers the job.
- #159 CanSNPer2: self.no_export was written and never read; the
  --no_snpfiles flag already reaches self.export.
- #160 CanSNPer2: create_mauve_command read self.query_name, which only
  run() happened to set, so calling align() directly died with
  AttributeError. The name is now taken from the query being aligned in
  align() itself, which also keeps the gap-N retry using the original
  sample name for its xmfa files.
- #161-#164 DatabaseConnection: removed the commented __name__ line, the
  superseded query loop in get_snps and the commented get_references stub
  (the SNPDatabase logger comment the sweep listed as #162 was removed too).
- #165 InitiateDatabase: unused sys/os/inspect/sqlite3 imports and two
  commented lines dropped; the CreateSNPDatabase call stays, its unused
  attribute does not.
- #166 ModifyDatabase: unused snp_annotation argument dropped and the
  commented-out AddReference class deleted, live add_genome and
  load_genome_reference_file already do that work.
- #167 ParseXMFA: self.export was never read (export is passed to the parse
  functions) and reverse_complement was never called; rcDict stays because
  find_snps uses it.
- #168 ReadCanSNP_tables: self.names and self.ids come from
  ReadTaxonomy.__init__ and are used by the inherited add_link/read_nodes,
  self.genomes was never used here.
- #169 ReadTaxonomyCanSNPer: removed self.qiime, the set_qiime() setter that
  only wrote it, and self.skipped; add_rank uses its own qiime parameter.
- #170 WriteTaxonomy: removed the unused dump_genomes() method and the
  matching unread dump_genomes= argument.
- #171 runMauve: RunMauve.run() never used its organism argument; the
  --organism flag is still accepted and now documented as ignored, since
  SNP finding is not implemented in that module.

Backups of the ten touched files are in
CanSNPer2/.fix-backups/2026-10-22-158-171-deadcode/.
